# Semantics:
# 1. THERMOSTAT_VERIFY can START only after actual measured boiler power is <100 W.
# 2. If power rises to >=100 W during an active verification, verification aborts and issues BOILER_OFF.
# 3. High-power heating (~1900 W) can no longer use THERMOSTAT_VERIFY to mask WAIT_IMPORT / planner-slot-end after normal run-lock.
# 4. Existing 10-minute low-power goal evidence in WW state is unchanged.